1
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,710
Mila drops an ice cube into her glass.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:06,067
Plop…

3
00:00:06,117 --> 00:00:07,565
and it comes back up!

4
00:00:07,615 --> 00:00:08,399
Ice floats.

5
00:00:09,235 --> 00:00:11,184
Yet a pebble sinks.

6
00:00:11,234 --> 00:00:12,763
A marble sinks.

7
00:00:12,813 --> 00:00:14,075
Why not ice?

8
00:00:14,895 --> 00:00:17,356
Noah has an idea: there's air inside,

9
00:00:17,406 --> 00:00:18,238
like a float!

10
00:00:18,288 --> 00:00:20,885
But this ice cube is clear, no bubbles…

11
00:00:20,935 --> 00:00:22,292
and it still floats.

12
00:00:23,062 --> 00:00:24,576
Discovery mission!

13
00:00:28,092 --> 00:00:28,733
Mini mode!

14
00:00:28,783 --> 00:00:32,051
In liquid water, the molecules are packed tight,

15
00:00:32,101 --> 00:00:35,488
and they move, jostle, and slide over each other.

16
00:00:36,274 --> 00:00:38,902
When it gets very cold, they slow down…

17
00:00:38,952 --> 00:00:40,961
and line up in a neat pattern.

18
00:00:41,011 --> 00:00:42,952
But look: lined up like this,

19
00:00:43,002 --> 00:00:44,581
they take up more room!

20
00:00:45,370 --> 00:00:47,248
So a piece of ice is lighter than

21
00:00:47,298 --> 00:00:49,234
a piece of water of the same size.

22
00:00:49,284 --> 00:00:51,044
And what is lighter than water…

23
00:00:51,094 --> 00:00:51,503
floats!

24
00:00:52,371 --> 00:00:54,324
It's the same for a giant iceberg:

25
00:00:54,374 --> 00:00:56,623
nine tenths are hidden under the water.

26
00:00:56,673 --> 00:00:57,851
We only see the tip.

27
00:00:58,648 --> 00:01:00,827
That's why ice floats on water.

28
00:01:02,630 --> 00:01:05,262
When water freezes, it takes up more room:

29
00:01:05,312 --> 00:01:07,866
ice is lighter than water, so it floats.

30
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:09,464
With an adult:

31
00:01:09,514 --> 00:01:13,714
fill a small bottle with water to the brim and put it in the freezer.

32
00:01:13,764 --> 00:01:16,659
Tomorrow, the ice will have swollen the bottle!

33
00:01:17,464 --> 00:01:19,741
And why is there day, then night?

34
00:01:19,791 --> 00:01:21,202
The answer tomorrow.
